10. Cycle Snapshot Query (Your Screenshot)

Your screenshot query is almost correct.

But yes — it should use participation table.

Corrected snapshot query:

INSERT INTO LH_CLO_CYCLE_ALLOCATION_SNAPSHOT
(
cycle_id,
hedge_id,
limit_id,
client_le_id,
program_id,
allocated_amount,
rating,
sector,
snapshot_time
)

SELECT
:cycle_id,
h.hedge_id,
h.limit_id,
h.client_le_id,
a.program_id,

SUM(
CASE
WHEN a.txn_type='INCREASE' THEN a.amount
WHEN a.txn_type='REDUCE' THEN -a.amount
END
),

inv.rating,
inv.sector,

CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

FROM LH_CLO_CYCLE_HEDGE_PARTICIPATION p

JOIN LH_CLO_HEDGE h
ON p.hedge_id = h.hedge_id

JOIN LH_CLO_HEDGE_ALLOCATIONS a
ON h.hedge_id = a.hedge_id

JOIN LH_LOAN_INVENTORY_MONTHLY inv
ON h.limit_id = inv.limit_id
AND h.client_le_id = inv.client_le_id

WHERE p.cycle_id = :cycle_id
AND a.allocation_cycle_id = :cycle_id

GROUP BY
h.hedge_id,
h.limit_id,
h.client_le_id,
a.program_id,
inv.rating,
inv.sector;


